sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User
    participant Runner as EdgeOptimizer Runner
    participant Store as Runner SQLite state.db
    participant WinUI as WinUI Settings client
    participant Legacy as Legacy Rust Settings
    participant Engine as EngineSvc (transitional)
    participant Crosshair as Crosshair worker
    participant Macro as Macro worker
    participant Broker as Privileged Broker (planned)

    %% Verified implementation: Runner owns startup, tray, and durable state.
    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over Runner,Store: Current implementation — Runner startup and state restoration
        Runner->>Store: Open state.db and apply schema migrations
        Runner->>Store: Import legacy JSON only when the database is empty
        Store-->>Runner: Profiles, active profile, and UI state snapshot
        Runner->>Runner: Create tray icon and transitional Settings pipe
        Note over Runner: Restoration does not activate profiles, terminate processes, or run cleanup.
    end

    %% The WinUI client is active for presentation but does not yet have a Runner transport.
    rect rgb(255, 248, 220)
        Note over User,WinUI: Current implementation — on-demand WinUI presentation
        User->>Runner: Choose Open Settings or double-click tray icon
        Runner->>Runner: Find existing Settings window
        alt Settings window exists
            Runner->>WinUI: Bring existing window to foreground
        else Settings window does not exist
            Runner->>WinUI: Start EdgeOptimizer.Settings.WinUI.exe
            WinUI->>WinUI: Create memory-only view models
        end
        Note over WinUI,Runner: The current WinUI client uses DisconnectedRunnerClient and does not request state or persist edits.

        User->>Runner: Single-click tray icon
        alt Legacy Rust Settings client is connected
            Runner->>Legacy: ShowFlyout via transitional Bincode pipe
        else No compatible pipe client is connected
            Runner->>WinUI: Start with --flyout-only
            Note over WinUI: Flyout IPC and WinUI 3 flyout handling remain planned.
        end
    end

    %% These protocols exist today but are transitional and are not the WinUI 3 contract.
    rect rgb(255, 240, 245)
        Note over Legacy,Engine: Current transitional orchestration path
        Legacy->>Runner: RequestState, profile edits, or orchestration command (Bincode pipe)
        Runner->>Store: Read snapshot or transact profile and active-state updates
        Store-->>Runner: Snapshot or persisted result
        Runner-->>Legacy: StateSnapshot or correlated event (Bincode pipe)

        Legacy->>Runner: Activate profile or request cleanup
        Runner->>Engine: ApplyProfile or RunCleanup (Bincode pipe)
        Note over Engine: Default pipe security and SYSTEM scheduled-task host are transitional.
        Engine->>Engine: Name-based process termination or cleanup
        Engine-->>Runner: Structured operation result
        opt Successful profile activation with overlay enabled
            Runner->>Crosshair: Start detached overlay process with image path and offsets
            Crosshair->>Crosshair: Render click-through, topmost layered window
        end
        Runner-->>Legacy: Optimization or cleanup result

        Note over Legacy,Macro: Existing Macro worker communication is direct and transitional.
        Legacy->>Macro: Private Bincode pipe
    end

    %% This section intentionally shows target behavior rather than claiming it exists.
    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over WinUI,Broker: Target architecture — planned, versioned contracts
        WinUI-->>Runner: Request snapshot and submit validated user intent (Protobuf over per-user pipe)
        Runner-->>WinUI: Snapshot, acknowledgement, progress, or structured error
        Runner->>Store: Own all durable profile and active-state changes

        Runner-->>Crosshair: Start, update, stop, acknowledgement, and render-error messages
        Runner-->>Macro: Configure, record, play, cancel, and worker-event messages
        Note over Crosshair,Macro: Workers remain unprivileged and never open durable state.

        Runner-->>Broker: Allowlisted machine-level operation with a versioned request
        Broker-->>Runner: Authorized, correlated result
        Note over Broker: SCM service verifies named-pipe peer identity and authorizes each operation.
        Note over Runner,Broker: User-specific cleanup remains in the verified interactive-user context, not SYSTEM.
    end
